Subject: [PATCH] Point Bolt URLs at boltapp.com (plugin 2.13.0)

Backport of bolt-magento2 PR #1973 onto the 2.13.0 release tag.

Rewrites the Bolt service hosts the plugin calls at runtime -- api, connect,
account, merchant and status -- from bolt.com to boltapp.com. Two changes are
additive rather than replacements, so the plugin keeps working on both apexes
during the cutover:

  * etc/csp_whitelist.xml gains a boltapp.com twin for every bolt.com host
    instead of swapping them, so a merchant's CSP allows either origin.
  * Helper/SSOHelper.php accepts boltapp.com issuers in addition to the
    bolt.com ones, so SSO tokens minted on either side still validate.

Helper/Config.php::validateCustomUrl is widened to bolt(app)?\.(me|com) so a
merchant-supplied custom URL on boltapp.com is not rejected.

Left alone on purpose: the www.bolt.com copyright headers, the
integrations@bolt.com contact address, docs.bolt.com help links
(docs.boltapp.com does not resolve), and CHANGELOG.md.

Apply from the plugin root:

    git apply bolt-magento2-2.13.0-boltapp-domains.patch
    # or, without git:
    patch -p1 < bolt-magento2-2.13.0-boltapp-domains.patch


Beyond the runtime hosts, this revision also moves every other bolt.com
reference that is not a dummy test fixture:

  * the copyright header in every file, tests included, reads
    https://www.boltapp.com
  * Helper/Cart.php detects Apple Pay's masked address by comparing the
    prefilled email against na@bolt.com; Bolt's checkout still sends that
    value, so the check now accepts both na@bolt.com and na@boltapp.com
  * etc/integration/config.xml lists integrations@boltapp.com (where the
    file exists at this version)
  * the admin help link in etc/adminhtml/system.xml points at
    help.boltapp.com, which resolves, instead of docs.bolt.com, which does
    not (where the link exists at this version)
  * dev@ and circleci@ addresses in the docker, operations and CI scripts
    move to boltapp.com; www.bolt.com URL fixtures in two unit tests follow
Files the plugin stores with Windows (CRLF) line endings are left out of this
patch. Their only change was the copyright header, and a hunk carrying CRLF
lines fails to apply wherever the store's copy, or this patch file, has been
normalised to LF -- an editor, a git checkout with autocrlf or text=auto, or a
copy and paste is enough.

Still left alone: etc/csp_whitelist.xml and Helper/SSOHelper.php keep their
bolt.com entries beside the boltapp.com ones on purpose, dummy test
addresses such as test@bolt.com stay, and CHANGELOG.md records history.

